       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. DA5GRPVERBS.
      *> DA5 - STRING / UNSTRING / INSPECT / ACCEPT INTO A GROUP WHOSE
      *> ONLY NON-CHARACTER LEAF IS BINARY. ALL FOUR LOUD-STAGED THE
      *> RECEIVER AS A "TIER-C BYTE ISLAND (NO WHOLE-GROUP CHARACTER
      *> IMAGE)" ON THE PRE-V59 PREDICATE, WHILE A GROUP *MOVE* INTO
      *> THE SAME RECEIVER ALREADY WORKED - SO FIVE VERBS DISAGREED
      *> ABOUT ONE RECEIVER.
      *>
      *> ⛔ THE INVARIANT THIS GOLDEN PINS: ALL OF THESE ARE POSITIONAL
      *> CHARACTER TRANSFERS INTO THE GROUP'S STORAGE, SO STRING AND
      *> UNSTRING MUST LAND BYTE-FOR-BYTE WHAT THE GROUP MOVE LANDS
      *> (14.9.25.4 GR4 - THE GROUP MOVE IS ALPHANUMERIC, "FILLED
      *> WITHOUT CONSIDERATION FOR THE INDIVIDUAL ITEMS"). LINES MOV,
      *> STR AND UNS BELOW MUST THEREFORE BE IDENTICAL. TESTING ONLY
      *> "IT NO LONGER THROWS" WOULD MISS A DIVERGENCE BETWEEN THEM.
      *>
      *> ⚠ AND WHY "BYTES ARE NOT TEXT" DOES *NOT* FORBID THIS: THAT
      *> RULE GOVERNS *RENDERING* A COMP LEAF'S VALUE AS TEXT (WHICH
      *> IS DisplayTextWidth's JOB, DA2). WRITING CHARACTERS
      *> POSITIONALLY OVER A GROUP'S BYTES IS A DIFFERENT OPERATION,
      *> AND IT IS EXACTLY WHAT A GROUP MOVE ALREADY DOES.
      *>
      *> THE INSPECT LINE IS THE SHARPEST CASE: THE BINARY LEAF HOLDS
      *> 0 (BYTES 00 00), WHICH ARE NOT SPACES, SO REPLACING SPACES
      *> MUST LEAVE THE LEAF UNTOUCHED AND CHANGE ONLY THE TEXT TAIL.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 GM.
          05 MN PIC S9(4) COMP VALUE 0.
          05 MA PIC X(3) VALUE "   ".
       01 GS.
          05 SN PIC S9(4) COMP VALUE 0.
          05 SA PIC X(3) VALUE "   ".
       01 GU.
          05 UN PIC S9(4) COMP VALUE 0.
          05 UA PIC X(3) VALUE "   ".
       01 GI.
          05 IN2 PIC S9(4) COMP VALUE 0.
          05 IA PIC X(3) VALUE "   ".
       01 SRC PIC X(5) VALUE "HELLO".
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE SRC TO GM.
           DISPLAY "MOV N=" MN " A=" MA.
           STRING SRC DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO GS.
           DISPLAY "STR N=" SN " A=" SA.
           UNSTRING SRC INTO GU.
           DISPLAY "UNS N=" UN " A=" UA.
      *> 00 00 20 20 20 -> REPLACE THE SPACES ONLY.
           INSPECT GI REPLACING ALL " " BY "x".
           DISPLAY "INS N=" IN2 " A=" IA.
           STOP RUN.
